2,Mwan,https://accentnetwork.com/mwan/,"April 22, 2025. Niger-Congo.Mwan, spoken by around 18,000 people in the Ivory Coast, is part of the Mande language family. It is culturally significant, especially in traditional ceremonies and rituals.",Mwan,Niger-Congo
3,"Mona, Mwan in Côte d'Ivoire people group profile | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/13784/IV,"Their language, Mwan, is a Southern Mande tongue of the Niger-Congo family, distinct from the dominant Manding languages of the north, though the Mwan Mona live in daily proximity to Koyaka, Sia, Malinke, and other neighbors.",Mwan,Niger-Congo
4,Caritive constructions in Mwan,https://shs.hal.science/halshs-03983676/document,"Abstract: The paper deals with strategies for expressing caritive meanings in Mwan (Niger-Congo < Mande < South Mande). The difference between the strategies used in Mwan and in some other languages of the same family (Gban, Looma, Bambara) is discussed.",Mwan,Niger-Congo
